  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-bundles",
      "text": "<!-- markdownlint-disable MD013 -->\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n**One-click, persona-based plugin bundles for DeepSeek Harness.** Choose how you work, review the included community plugins, and install the complete toolkit from one card.\n\n[Website](https://dshbundles.com) · [Plugin market](https://dshmarket.com/) · [Bundle catalog](data/bundles.json)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dshbundles\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`, then open **Settings → Plugin Bundles**.\n\nInstall a specific official or verified community bundle directly from a terminal:\n\n```sh\nnpx -y dshbundles@latest install developer --profile web\n```\n\nSafely uninstall the same bundle:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y dshbundles@latest uninstall developer --profile web\n```\n\nAdopt a complete legacy install that is shown as unmanaged from the UI, or run:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Successful installs write an ownership ledger to `.dsh-bundles/state.json` in the target profile. Uninstall removes only packages installed exclusively by that bundle; pre-existing packages and packages still referenced by another bundle are preserved. Use `list` and `status [bundle-id]` to inspect installation and management state. Legacy adoption requires explicit confirmation and claims packages without another ownership record; it never happens automatically, so independently installed packages are not silently made removable."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "For source testing before a release, use `dsh plugin --profile web add --allow-build=dshbundles github:LM20230311/dsh-bundles#main`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use a bundle",
      "text": "1. Click anywhere on a persona card to expand its plugin list.\n2. Click a plugin row to inspect its description, source, repository, and market metadata.\n3. Click **Install all** to install the complete bundle and watch live progress; afterwards, use **Safe uninstall** from the same card. For a complete legacy install, use **Manage legacy install** first."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use a bundle",
      "text": "Already-installed plugins are skipped. Before changing the profile, dsh-bundles snapshots `package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml`; if a required plugin fails, it restores the previous dependency state.\n\nEach pnpm command has a three-minute default deadline. A timeout terminates the complete process group and enters the existing rollback path instead of leaving the UI stuck on “installing”. Set `DSHBUNDLES_PNPM_TIMEOUT_MS` to override the deadline in milliseconds on slower networks."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you get",
      "text": "| Capability | Details |\n| --- | --- |\n| Persona bundles | 6 curated toolkits and 29 community plugins for developers, creators, designers, students, researchers, and fun |\n| One-click workflow | Full-card expansion, bundle preview, one-click install, safe uninstall, live progress, and per-plugin results |\n| Plugin details | Install source and repository links for every catalog entry; richer descriptions, author, downloads, stars, categories, and screenshots when dshmarket is installed |\n| Safe recovery | Skips installed packages, preserves pre-existing/shared plugins, and rolls back failed install or uninstall operations |\n| Shared catalog | Verified community bundles come from dshbundles.com; [`data/bundles.json`](data/bundles.json) remains the offline fallback |"
    },
    {
      "section": "dshmarket integration",
      "text": "[dshmarket](https://github.com/dsh-market/dsh-market) is optional. Install it directly from the bundle page, then use localized dshmarket detail links to inspect, update, or remove individual plugins. Remote community bundles are accepted only when every npm package is present in dshmarket's curated registry."
    },
    {
      "section": "Submit a bundle",
      "text": "Publish a community bundle at [dshbundles.com/publish](https://dshbundles.com/publish). The site validates every package against dshmarket's curated registry and exposes verified bundles to the same catalog consumed inside DSH.\n\nTo propose or update an official built-in bundle:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Submit a bundle",
      "text": "1. Edit [`data/bundles.json`](data/bundles.json).\n2. Give every bundle a unique `id`, localized `persona` and `tagline`, and at least one plugin.\n3. Use `target` for GitHub or tarball installation sources when the plugin name is not directly installable.\n4. Run `npm run check`, then open a pull request."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run check\nnpm run audit:bundles\n```\n\n`npm run check` runs both TypeScript projects, the installer/route tests, and the client bundle build. `npm run audit:bundles` checks npm availability, DSH manifests, release activity, and weekly download signals for every official plugin, then updates [`reports/bundle-audit.md`](reports/bundle-audit.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE) · [dshbundles.com](https://dshbundles.com)"
    }
  ],
